# Git runs this from the repository root. The desktop app is its own yarn project, and its
# lint-staged config reaches only files under desktop/, so a commit that stages none is a no-op.
# --no-stash: lint-staged backs up through git stash create/store, and the house rule bans any git stash, for
# any reason - the stack is shared by every checkout and session. Without it lint-staged still hides a partially
# staged file's unstaged changes, through a patch file of its own (17.5.1 gitWorkflow.js, prepare); what goes is only
# the backup, and with it the undo when a task fails.
# --relative --max-arg-length 8000: Windows caps a command line at 8,191 characters, and lint-staged splits a
# long file list only when --max-arg-length is set (17.5.1 getSpawnedTasks.js; unset, it never chunks). Relative
# paths keep each chunk short. A 91-file commit failed without them on 2026-09-25 (the fleet baseline).
cd desktop && yarn lint-staged --no-stash --relative --max-arg-length 8000
